# Cloudless Sky: limits the Docker build context to the source tree, so an
# image built from a working copy matches one built from a fresh clone.
#
# - The image installs its own dependencies (`pnpm install --frozen-lockfile`).
# - The Dockerfile writes its own .env from build arguments; `expo export`
#   would also load any local .env.* file, baking its settings into the bundle.
# - bskyweb embeds everything under static/ and templates/ (go:embed), so
#   locally generated web and embed build output must stay out.
# - No build step reads .git, and its churn would invalidate the layer cache.
.git
**/node_modules
.env*
bskyweb/.env*
dist
web-build
bskyweb/bskyweb
bskyweb/embedr
bskyweb/static/_expo
bskyweb/static/assets
bskyweb/static/js/*.js
bskyweb/static/js/*.map
bskyweb/static/js/*.js.LICENSE.txt
bskyweb/static/css/*.css
bskyweb/static/css/*.map
bskyweb/static/css/*.css.LICENSE.txt
bskyweb/static/media/*.png
bskyweb/static/embed/*.html
bskyweb/static/embed/assets/*.js
bskyweb/static/embed/assets/*.css
bskyweb/templates/scripts.html
bskyweb/templates/fonts.html
bskyweb/templates/*-embed.html
bskyweb/embedr-static/post-*.js
bskyweb/embedr-static/post-*.css
bskyweb/embedr-static/index-*.js
bskyweb/embedr-static/polyfills-*.js
